      - id: "wp-ancient"
        name: "W.P. Ancient Weapons Program"
        skills:
          - { choose: 3, from: ["W.P. Blunt", "W.P. Chain", "W.P. Knife", "W.P. Sword", "W.P. Staff", "W.P. Targeting", "W.P. Paired Weapons"], note: "Printed 28: select three; the seven are enumerated on printed 29. A W.P. has no percentage, so the educational bonus does not apply." }
  occ_related_skills: { count: 0 }
  occ_secondary_skills: { count: 10 }
---

## Lore

Rolled 01-09 on the Educational Level table, printed 27. The level fixes three things: a one-time bonus of +5% applied to every scholastic skill, 2 skill programs, and 10 secondary skills.

Heroes Unlimited puts education in the occupation slot rather than giving a character a job: what a hero did before the powers arrived is how well they read, not what they do for a living. Two Power Categories never roll here at all - Special Training and Physical Training print their own skill packages, and each of those is its own class.

**The percentages are this book''s, not the catalog''s.** Heroes Unlimited prints its own base for every skill and they differ from the shared catalog''s nearly everywhere - 29 of the 33 names that appear in both, measured against production on 2026-09-14. Computer Operation is 60% here and 40% there. Every named skill above therefore states this book''s number with the educational bonus already added. A choice group cannot do that, because its bonus adds to whatever the picked row already holds; see `BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md` F83.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'hu-edu-high-school');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'hu-edu-high-school';

